(EXP-81: any base from 2 through 36 is supported; digits above 9 use the
 letters a-z, case-insensitively.
 Both ends of the range are recorded, the case-insensitivity is recorded as
 `ZZ` and `zz` giving the same number, and a middle base is recorded in both
 the fused and the spaced spelling so the two are known to agree on a base
 nobody aliased.
 EXP-100 records what happens outside the range.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-81.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   3
   1295
   1295
   1295
   14167554
   14167554
   7
)
Print "11" as a base 2 number.
Print "ZZ" as a base 36 number.
Print "zz" as a base 36 number.
Print "zz" as a base36 number.
Print "hello" as a base 30 number.
Print "HELLO" as a base 30 number.
Print "7" as a base 8 number.
